### Conclusion

The backward trace from 2008 yields a unique chain:

$$1919 \xrightarrow{s=20} 1939 \xrightarrow{s=22} 1961 \xrightarrow{s=17} 1978 \xrightarrow{s=25} 2003 \xrightarrow{s=5} 2008$$

**Verification:** $s(1919)=20$, $1919+20=1939$ ✓; $s(1939)=22$, $1939+22=1961$ ✓; $s(1961)=17$, $1961+17=1978$ ✓; $s(1978)=25$, $1978+25=2003$ ✓; $s(2003)=5$, $2003+5=2008$ ✓.

Since 1919 has no predecessor, this chain cannot be extended backward. Since every step has a unique predecessor (except 2008, whose other branch through 1985 terminates immediately), no longer chain exists.

The greatest possible $n$ is $\boxed{6}$.

